HST Office: VBScript.RegExp and Scripting.FileSystemObject on every platform.

Measured on real macro files: 10% use FileSystemObject and 6% RegExp, and neither existed off Windows
(CreateObject failed, New Scripting.FileSystemObject too). basic now has its own objects: RegExp
(Pattern, Global, IgnoreCase, MultiLine, Test, Execute, Replace, Match and SubMatches, through ICU);
FileSystemObject (exists, name helpers, File, Folder, Files, SubFolders, copy, move, delete, create,
CreateTextFile, OpenTextFile) and TextStream. Backslash paths work on Linux and macOS. New
VBA.Collection is the same as New Collection.
The new files are for HST Office under MPL-2.0, like the files around them.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/vba-corpus/regression_cases.py (regexp-*, fso-* cases).
